WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.750
Somehow, most likely through some nefarious
means, a fateful postcard had been sent to

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.900
one of the residents of the murky, mysterious
Aranearum island.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:17.210
Living on this particular island was already
a strange and scary enough existence, given

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.340
the horrors the inhabitants of Aranearum shared
their home with.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:27.350
But perhaps the only thing just as horrible
as life on that island was being sent a postcard.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.449
Sure, that doesn’t sound all that horrible.

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:35.680
Postcards are usually used to show a corner
of the world far away, and extend well wishes

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.950
from friends or relatives on vacations.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:45.700
But ordinarily, postcards don’t depict a
photo of SCP-096, with the words ‘Wish he

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.550
was there’ scrawled on the other side.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:54.510
From its containment cell at the SCP Foundation,
the Shy Guy instantly sensed that somebody,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.300
somewhere, had seen a picture of its face.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:05.030
Breaking down into an enraged fit of homicidal
insecurity, SCP-096 immediately broke from

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:10.670
its containment chamber and made a cross-country
beeline, heading straight for Aranearum at

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.820
anomalously accelerated speeds.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:19.030
Little did the creature, or the Foundation,
know, that the Shy Guy was being led straight

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.189
into a trap.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.299
And the poor island resident who had received
the chilling postcard?

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:27.710
Well, they were unlucky enough to be the bait.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:32.261
While the SCP Foundation started frantically
trying to track down where it had gone, the

00:01:32.261 --> 00:01:37.619
Shy Guy had already made its way to a wooden
cabin belonging to the unfortunate postcard

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:38.619
recipient.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:45.040
Emerging from the now-emptied home, once the
owner was no more, SCP-096 would have returned

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.780
to his cell just as quickly as he left.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:52.000
That is, if he wasn’t the only monstrous
creature on the island.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.310
A loud and sudden noise caught the creature’s
attention, the sound of an old steam train

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.310
whistle.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:04.030
It rang out once, from somewhere off in the
distance, but there was so much thick fog

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:09.300
hanging in the air around Aranearum that it
was almost impossible to see anything, especially

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.910
with how dark it was.

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.170
The second time the whistle sounded, it was
closer.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:20.470
But there was another sound too and not the
loud chugging of a steam engine that you would

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.470
expect.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:26.540
It was an erratic, heavy thudding, the noise
of lots of somethings drumming against the

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.769
ground, causing the earth itself to shudder.

00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:30.769
Legs.

00:02:30.769 --> 00:02:36.890
They were the steps of multiple huge legs,
crawling across the surface of the island:

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.370
heading straight towards SCP-096.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:44.890
A third, piercing whistle rang out, even closer
still.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:50.709
This time, the orange glow of a light could
be seen, dulled by the surrounding fog, but

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:54.599
getting brighter and clearer as it came closer.

00:02:54.599 --> 00:02:59.670
The light was casting shadows against the
dark fog, long, spindly shapes of spidery

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:00.730
appendages.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:07.370
Until, before the Shy Guy’s eyes, a creature
of pure nightmares came bursting out of the

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.370
fog.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.900
It was a monstrous sight, even to SCP-096.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:18.940
Its body was the red front engine of an old-fashioned
steam train, hoisted off the ground by four

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:24.510
pairs of enormous black, spindly, spider-like
legs that propelled the beast forwards at

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.349
a terrifying speed.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:31.250
Able to move without the limitations of needing
to follow a railroad track, the monster was

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:38.080
barreling towards SCP-096, with a twisted
smile on its grotesque face.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:44.330
At the front of the locomotive was its circular
face, with unnaturally white eyes and a mouth

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:49.360
that sported rows of razor-sharp teeth, all
covered in blood.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:55.019
This hellish abomination, a being that was
part steam engine and part giant spider, was

00:03:55.019 --> 00:04:01.450
the Terror of Aranearum himself: the carnivorous
Choo-Choo Charles.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.310
Seeing Charles racing towards them on its
eight spider legs would be enough to make

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:09.879
anyone freeze up and stop in their tracks
out of sheer terror.

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:13.930
And SCP-096 was compelled to do the same.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.829
Except the terrifying train creature’s pale
eyes were looking directly at the Shy Guy

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:22.630
as Charles sized the anomaly up as its next
meal.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:29.169
He was looking at it, and that meant SCP-096
had to kill him.

00:04:29.169 --> 00:04:32.060
The question was, how could it?

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:37.880
How could the skinny, spindly humanoid hope
to even fight something like Choo-Choo Charles?

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.500
He was much bigger, even more fearsome…
but as quick as Charles could move on his

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:47.740
spidery legs, he wasn’t faster than SCP-096.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.190
In the blink of an eye, the Shy Guy raced
off shrieking and sobbing in despair, leaving

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:58.520
Charles to continue roaming his island territory
in search of other human inhabitants to terrorize.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:04.020
SCP-096 had retreated to some nearby woods,
quick enough to move out of Charles’ path

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.699
somewhere it could hide, for now.

00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:12.820
But the Shy Guy could feel a familiar, painful
feeling, almost pulling him back towards Choo-Choo

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.900
Charles, right back into harm’s way.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:22.601
SCP-096 possessed an inescapable compulsion
to kill anyone who looked at its face, and

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:27.150
that seemed to include horrifying part train,
part spider hybrids.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:33.260
It was a fact of the Shy Guy’s very existence,
he had to go after whoever looked at him and

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.260
make them pay.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:38.850
In fact, it took all the creature’s own
strength not to instantly rush back over to

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:44.900
Charles to try; SCP-096 knew that, if it did,
then there was little chance it would survive

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.550
coming face to train face with the Terror
of Aranearum.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:53.630
However, it was while watching Choo-Choo Charles
from a safe distance, seeing him crawl across

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:58.830
the landscape on his multiple legs, that SCP-096
noticed something.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:03.490
It was another light obscured by the fog,
but this one was much higher up.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:08.560
One could almost mistake it for the moon,
if it wasn’t getting closer, all while accompanied

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.509
by the sound of whirring rotors.

00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:15.980
While the Shy Guy had been evading Choo-Choo
Charles, the SCP Foundation had been tirelessly

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.880
trying to track down its location.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:22.560
And now, they’d found their runaway anomaly
here on Aranearum island.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.729
As the chopper carrying the Mobile Task Force
drew nearer, the tyrannical train turned and

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:27.910
took notice.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:32.940
To SCP-096, the Foundation’s arrival could
have meant a way home and away from the spidery

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.250
steam engine.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.900
But to Charles, the approaching chopper meant
only one thing: a new source of food.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:40.900
“Captain!”

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.700
one of the MTF troops aboard the chopper called
over his headset.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:44.700
“What is it?

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.950
Do we have eyes on SCP-096?”

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:49.860
the captain replied, before realizing what
he’d said.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.610
“Well, not ‘eyes-on’ because then it
would’ve jumped up onto the chopper and

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.610
killed us all.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.810
I mean, is there any sign of SCP-096 on the
island?”

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:59.849
“Negative, sir, although you should probably
see this!”

00:06:59.849 --> 00:07:01.470
the soldier replied.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:05.389
Begrudgingly, the captain unbuckled himself
from his seat and snatched the Foundation

00:07:05.389 --> 00:07:09.849
operative’s binoculars, using them to look
down at Aranearum below.

00:07:09.849 --> 00:07:14.539
It didn’t take him long to spot the massive,
multi-legged monstrosity that was Choo-Choo

00:07:14.539 --> 00:07:19.400
Charles, who had fallen still, waiting for
the chopper to descend low enough for him

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.400
to reach.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.770
“Good gravy, what on Earth is that thing?!”

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:25.930
the captain exclaimed, before taking another
look through the binoculars.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:31.470
“Is that… wait, what is an instance of
SCP-2086 doing out here?”

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:37.030
SCP-2086 was an infamous anomalous species
that the Foundation had encountered before.

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:41.520
Much like Charles, they were arthropod-like
creatures with multiple long legs that protruded

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.729
from a body resembling a man-made mode of
transport.

00:07:44.729 --> 00:07:50.270
However, SCP-2086’s usually took on the
appearance of buses while in vehicle form.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:54.570
“Sir, I don’t think it’s an SCP-2086,”
the lookout replied.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:58.360
“To me, it looks much more like an instance
of SCP-3023.”

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.729
“Impossible, all the way out here?”

00:08:00.729 --> 00:08:01.849
the captain retorted.

00:08:01.849 --> 00:08:04.580
“We’re nowhere near the region where that
anomaly occurs.”

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.310
“It could have scurried its way from Germany
and taken nest here, sir,” the trooper responded.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:15.259
Yet another anomaly that Choo-Choo Charles
bore a striking resemblance to, SCP-3023 was

00:08:15.259 --> 00:08:20.389
a rare phenomenon that was known to occur
at random, but was limited to a specific area

00:08:20.389 --> 00:08:21.950
of Central Germany.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:27.199
The effect of this phenomenon caused ordinary,
everyday inanimate objects, of any shape or

00:08:27.199 --> 00:08:32.589
size, to suddenly turn into aggressive spiders,
sporting eight legs that grew from whatever

00:08:32.589 --> 00:08:36.000
was affected by SCP-3023.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:42.020
Perhaps Choo-Choo Charles was indeed an instance
of SCP-3023, or some distant evolutionary

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.709
offshoot of SCP-2086.

00:08:43.709 --> 00:08:46.930
It was hard to say for sure.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:52.080
The only thing for sure was that Charles was
a man-eating beast, more so than an insidious

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.160
villain.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:59.170
And being so highly territorial, he considered
the entire island of Aranearum to be his natural

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:02.350
habitat; and his hunting ground.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:07.089
Anything that arrived in his vicinity was
prey to the terrifying train, and his ravenous

00:09:07.089 --> 00:09:12.460
craving for human flesh meant he was ready
to attack the descending SCP Foundation chopper.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:15.110
“Alright, let’s go, go, go!”

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:19.519
the MTF captain called to his troops, signaling
them to start rappelling out of the helicopter

00:09:19.519 --> 00:09:20.529
and down to the island.

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:25.390
“Keep your SCRAMBLE goggles on max, we still
need to recapture SCP-096, but first priority

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.940
is taking down this big, ugly beast!”

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:32.500
Wearing goggles specially designed to distort
the Shy Guy from their view, the team began

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.540
abseiling out of the aircraft.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:37.290
But Choo-Choo Charles was already waiting
for them.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:42.760
Rearing back on its four back legs, the nightmarish
train-spider swiped at the descending MTF

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.760
operatives.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:48.650
What first seemed like an instinctive, uncoordinated
assault quickly became precise and relentless

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:52.970
strikes as Charles’ sliced through some
of the cables the MTF troops were using to

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:54.300
rappel down.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.440
Their lifeline cut, the unlucky Foundation
operatives plummeted from mid-air, right down

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:03.470
towards where the Terror of Aranearum was
waiting for them to fall.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:07.970
A few of the MTFs made it to the ground alive,
and immediately began retaliating against

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:09.370
Choo-Choo Charles.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:13.450
The gunfire from their weapons flickered all
around the carnivorous creature, but their

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:17.380
bullets could barely chip the red paintwork
on his steam train body.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:22.579
Dashing towards his helpless human prey on
his many legs, Charles began to feast.

00:10:22.579 --> 00:10:27.530
Then suddenly, something started pulling at
one of his huge spider legs, pulling Charles

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:32.490
back moments before he had a chance to claim
his latest victim, the captain of the Foundation’s

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.490
MTF.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:39.339
It was SCP-096, having zipped out of hiding
and shrieking wildly as it used all of its

00:10:39.339 --> 00:10:43.140
strength to wrench at one of Choo-Choo Charles’
multiple limbs.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:47.720
Angered that it couldn’t reach the MTF Captain,
the part spider, part train hybrid stomped

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:52.560
the leg that was being pulled, in a successful
attempt to free itself from the Shy Guy’s

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.560
grip.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:58.840
But in the same instant, SCP-096 used its
anomalous speed to reappear in front of the

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.260
already angered locomotive monster.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:06.329
With his railroad rage about to reach its
breaking point, Charles entered into a relentless

00:11:06.329 --> 00:11:11.480
rampage, making quick work of the leftover
MTF troops before setting his sights squarely

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.950
on SCP-096.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.420
But doing that was his biggest mistake.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:19.870
Now Choo-Choo Charles had seen the Shy Guy
twice.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:24.430
And to the insecure anomaly, that meant Charles
had to go.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:30.090
Traveling faster than even the multi-legged
monstrosity could perceive, SCP-096 began

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.930
racing towards Choo-Choo-Charles’ many legs.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:36.690
The Shy Guy had realized that it didn’t
stand a chance of dealing with the Terror

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:41.459
of Aranearum the same way it handled all the
others that saw its face.

00:11:41.459 --> 00:11:47.570
So, instead, it had settled on a new approach,
specially tailored to take down the spider-legged

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:48.830
steam engine.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:55.570
One by one, SCP-096 started knocking Charles’
many legs out from underneath him, effectively

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:58.980
tripping him up over and over again.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:03.720
The Shy Guy moved so quick that the cumbersome
Charles could barely react in time, having

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:08.500
one leg after the other knocked out from beneath
him, causing him to tumble to the ground.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.700
Normally, Choo-Choo Charles was smart enough
to retreat if he encountered something that

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.029
could fight back.

00:12:14.029 --> 00:12:18.100
If he was injured badly enough, the spider-like
creature would scuttle out of harm’s way

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.019
in order to heal his wounds.

00:12:20.019 --> 00:12:25.220
But the rage at being constantly tripped up
by SCP-096 was distracting Charles from the

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.209
Shy Guy’s true ploy.

00:12:27.209 --> 00:12:32.740
With every leg it knocked out from underneath
the spidery steam train, SCP-096 had been

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:36.100
gradually directing Charles towards a nearby
gorge.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:40.670
With a terrifying burst of anomalous speed,
the Shy Guy caused Choo-Choo Charles to topple

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:45.800
over sideways, rolling over himself until
he landed upside down in the bottom of the

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:46.959
rocky gorge.

00:12:46.959 --> 00:12:52.200
The multi-legged locomotive monster’s spindly
legs flailed desperately as he tried to reposition

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.459
himself, but with no luck.

00:12:54.459 --> 00:13:01.330
SCP-096 had managed what first seemed to be
impossible, and beaten the Terror of Aranearum,

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:03.399
Choo-Choo Charles.

00:13:03.399 --> 00:13:05.910
Or for now, at least…

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:14.240
Now go and check out “SCP-096 VS SCP-343”
and “SCP-096 VS SCP-106” for more!

